meta {
  name: Read one book
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/books/{{bookId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200, or 404 when nothing holds that identifier.

  Deactivated books are included here, unlike in the listing. A caller asking for a specific
  book by identifier is not browsing, and hiding a withdrawn title from them would only make
  it look deleted - which is the one thing this API never does.

  Read straight from PostgreSQL rather than through Redis: a book by identifier is a
  primary-key lookup, and caching it would add an invalidation path for no measurable gain.
}
